
<p>Andrew Webster, The Verge (gift link):</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>How do you follow a game like <em>Grand Theft Auto V</em>? Thirteen years
ago, Rockstar’s crime-fueled epic went on to redefine what an
open-world game could be and became an enormous success, selling
more than 230 million copies across three generations of game
consoles. It sits just behind <em>Tetris</em> and <em>Minecraft</em> on the list
of the best-selling games of all time, and <a href="https://www.afp.com/en/grand-theft-auto-online-top-video-games-roleplay-cash-cow">its lucrative online
mode</a> has helped it remain popular for well over a decade.</p>

<p>That level of success has allowed Rockstar to take its time with a
sequel, which has further increased the hype around the next
<em>GTA</em>. A series of <a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/984959/gta-vi-leaks-rockstar-games-official-statement-heartbreaking">major leaks</a> and <a href="https://www.theverge.com/news/816005/grand-theft-auto-vi-gta-g-delayed-november-2026">delays</a> only
exacerbated this. At a time when <a href="https://www.theverge.com/column/1022402/new-zelda-and-gta-represent-a-games-industry-that-no-longer-exists">much of the video game industry
is struggling</a>, <a href="https://www.theverge.com/column/983410/grand-theft-auto-vi-exists-in-its-own-universe">the next edition of <em>GTA</em> stands
alone</a>, a cultural moment so big (<a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/1025415/the-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time-review-nintendo-switch-2">almost</a>) <a href="https://www.theverge.com/entertainment/944229/grand-theft-auto-6-release-calendar-summer-game-fest">everybody
has been forced to get out of the way</a>. The buildup to <em>Grand
Theft Auto VI</em>’s launch is unlike anything the game industry has
ever seen.</p>

<p>Even more remarkable? The game was actually worth the wait.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>The entire tech world is celebrating something today. On one side (avarice, hype) the Anthropic IPO. On the other (fun, mayhem) GTA 6. I briefly watched my son play last night after it came out at midnight. It looks incredible and fun as hell.</p>

